---
title: Consumer - what happens to each zip in the inbox
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> Arrived : watchdog event or timed scan<br/>(.partial files ignored)
    Arrived --> Arrived : still changing<br/>(settle_seconds)
    Arrived --> Duplicate : same sha256 seen before
    Arrived --> Verifying

    Verifying --> Failed : cannot decrypt, unsigned or untrusted signature,<br/>checksum or count mismatch, plaintext when encryption required
    Verifying --> Skipped : domain not accepted
    Verifying --> Stale : older than the zip already<br/>applied for this domain
    Verifying --> Processing

    state Processing {
        direction LR
        [*] --> OpenIAM : CONSUMER_TARGET=openiam
        [*] --> Plan : CONSUMER_TARGET=ad
        OpenIAM --> [*] : records upserted,<br/>then instructions
        Plan --> [*]
    }

    Processing --> Applied : every record / change done
    Processing --> Partial : some failed (retried with the next zip,<br/>or "apply again" in oversight)
    Processing --> Planned : AD mode dry_run
    Processing --> AwaitingApproval : AD mode approve,<br/>or auto above max_changes_auto
    Processing --> Retry : AD unreachable<br/>(file stays in the inbox)
    AwaitingApproval --> Applied : operator approves<br/>(re-planned against AD first)
    AwaitingApproval --> Rejected : operator rejects

    Failed --> [*] : moved to failed/
    Duplicate --> [*] : archive/DOMAIN/
    Skipped --> [*] : archive/DOMAIN/
    Stale --> [*] : archive/DOMAIN/
    Applied --> [*] : archive/DOMAIN/
    Partial --> [*] : archive/DOMAIN/
    Planned --> [*] : archive/DOMAIN/
    Rejected --> [*] : archive/DOMAIN/
    Retry --> Arrived : next scan
